<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Science and technology news and headlines - RFI</title><description>Follow all scientifical and technological news on RFI.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-technology/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:43:23 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-technology/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>'An honour to be chosen': Italian astronaut on piloting Nasa lunar mission</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260627-an-honour-to-be-chosen-italian-astronaut-on-piloting-nasa-lunar-mission-artemis-iii</link><description>
Italian astronaut Luca Parmitano will be the first European to participate in Nasa's lunar programme, as part of the Artemis III mission in 2027. He spoke to RFI about the challenges of such a mission, and the risks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e152334-651d-11f1-b62a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-09T195020Z-660891222-RC2BQLAWXJGZ-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-MOON-ARTEMIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e152334-651d-11f1-b62a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-09T195020Z-660891222-RC2BQLAWXJGZ-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-MOON-ARTEMIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5394b04-6fce-11f1-af7b-23076c0404aa</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 13:34:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e152334-651d-11f1-b62a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-09T195020Z-660891222-RC2BQLAWXJGZ-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-MOON-ARTEMIS.jpg">REUTERS - Antranik Tavitian</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Current Europe heatwave 'impossible' without human-induced climate change</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260626-europe-heatwave-virtually-impossible-without-human-caused-climate-change</link><description>
A study comparing the heatwave that has swept across Europe this week with heatwaves in 1976 and 2003 has found that human-caused climate change is "unequivocally" responsible for the extreme heat over the last week – with France recording its hottest day since records began in 1947 on Wednesday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/027f5fe8-70c3-11f1-8b7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8246NT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/027f5fe8-70c3-11f1-8b7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8246NT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a7bd136-7125-11f1-9a8e-01fd4a7e37ad</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 07:06:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/027f5fe8-70c3-11f1-8b7d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8246NT.jpg">AFP - DIMITAR DILKOFF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>France powers ahead in AI development, with more funding, public service tools</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260616-france-powers-ahead-in-ai-development-with-more-funding-public-service-tools</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu announced on Tuesday a further investment of €655 million to accelerate the development of artificial intelligence as well as an AI programme for public service employees. France is keen to build strategic autonomy in the face of competition from China and the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/690e9d74-d1e9-11f0-8705-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-01-16T232641Z-206750846-RC2CJ5A8JCG8-RTRMADP-3-AUSTRALIA-AI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/690e9d74-d1e9-11f0-8705-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-01-16T232641Z-206750846-RC2CJ5A8JCG8-RTRMADP-3-AUSTRALIA-AI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0f02b8e4-6963-11f1-8a71-2962102ed5b9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 16 Jun 2026 11:26:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/690e9d74-d1e9-11f0-8705-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-01-16T232641Z-206750846-RC2CJ5A8JCG8-RTRMADP-3-AUSTRALIA-AI.jpg">REUTERS - DADO RUVIC</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>France shoots for the stars with back-to-back space firsts</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260603-france-shoots-for-the-stars-with-back-to-back-space-firsts</link><description>
Two French astronauts will travel to space next year under a new deal between France and US company Vast, with one set to remain aboard what would be the world's first commercial space station.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ee4e88a-5e5e-11f1-8d4e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4NX49E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ee4e88a-5e5e-11f1-8d4e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4NX49E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33e87fa6-5e80-11f1-a9e0-1740558f1e5a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 03 Jun 2026 08:43:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8ee4e88a-5e5e-11f1-8d4e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4NX49E.jpg">© AFP/Ludovic Marin</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Monkey business: artist chimps paint in their own style, study shows</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260524-monkey-business-artist-chimps-splash-out-in-their-own-style-study-shows</link><description>
Several studies conducted in captivity have demonstrated that chimpanzees, like other great apes, enjoy painting and drawing. But new resreach led by French and Japanese primatologists has shown that they each have their own drawing style – and that it can evolve and improve over time.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1cf8884e-55d0-11f1-ada5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-APP2001050543452.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1cf8884e-55d0-11f1-ada5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-APP2001050543452.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55636582-55d0-11f1-8d6d-abfaa44c6f6f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 24 May 2026 14:41:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1cf8884e-55d0-11f1-ada5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-APP2001050543452.jpg">© AFP - Alain Jocard</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Child vaccine catch-up drive on course to hit target, says UN</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260424-child-vaccine-catch-up-drive-on-course-to-hit-target-says-united-nations</link><description>
A three-year effort to immunise children who missed routine vaccinations due to the Covid-19 crisis is on course to reach the 21 million target, the United Nations has said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a9395608-c153-11ee-b481-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-01-17T161802Z_666679650_RC2PJ5ANQJ64_RTRMADP_3_ZAMBIA-CHOLERA.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a9395608-c153-11ee-b481-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-01-17T161802Z_666679650_RC2PJ5ANQJ64_RTRMADP_3_ZAMBIA-CHOLERA.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">134ee96a-3fa9-11f1-9535-997757562443</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2026 07:24:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a9395608-c153-11ee-b481-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-01-17T161802Z_666679650_RC2PJ5ANQJ64_RTRMADP_3_ZAMBIA-CHOLERA.JPG">REUTERS - NAMUKOLO SIYUMBWA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Artemis mission takes historic step as astronauts conduct lunar flyby</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/artemis-mission-takes-historic-step-as-astronauts-conduct-lunar-flyby-moon-space-science</link><description>
The astronauts of NASA’s Artemis mission have reached a crucial moment in their journey to the Moon, entering the final phase before their historic lunar flyby.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e260c594-319d-11f1-8d69-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Orion-Spaceship.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e260c594-319d-11f1-8d69-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Orion-Spaceship.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8aab2bc2-318f-11f1-bc5a-a9ecaf3f7d88</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 10:14:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e260c594-319d-11f1-8d69-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Orion-Spaceship.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - NASA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Artemis II: humanity's return to the Moon reaches the launch pad</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260318-artemis-ii-humanity-s-return-to-the-moon-reaches-the-launch-pad</link><description>
When European Space Agency astronaut Luca Parmitano commanded the International Space Station in 2019, Christina Koch was his flight engineer. The pair spent six months together in orbit before returning to Earth on the same Soyuz spacecraft. Now Koch is preparing to fly to the Moon, and Parmitano says the mission she is about to undertake will change everything.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/78b26894-22d6-11f1-b6bd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-932u3a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/78b26894-22d6-11f1-b6bd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-932u3a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6fe987e-22d7-11f1-8b8a-bd0440a37c81</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 15:00:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/78b26894-22d6-11f1-b6bd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-932u3a8.jpg">© Jim WATSON / AFP</source><dc:creator>Dhananjay Khadilikar with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>French start-up raises $1 billion to shift AI research into 'high gear'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260310-french-startup-raises-1-billion-to-shift-ai-research-into-high-gear</link><description>
French artificial intelligence start-up AMI said on Tuesday it had raised $1 billion (€890 billion) to develop AI systems designed to understand the physical world “in the way animals and humans do”, rather than relying on language-based models such as ChatGPT. The company expects to produce “fairly universal intelligent systems” within five years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8173428e-c627-11f0-8a97-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-11-19T215040Z-1288817315-RC2JFCAAYKQX-RTRMADP-3-META-PLATFORMS-YANN-LECUN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8173428e-c627-11f0-8a97-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-11-19T215040Z-1288817315-RC2JFCAAYKQX-RTRMADP-3-META-PLATFORMS-YANN-LECUN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6293f3a6-1c6f-11f1-b83e-937dca7cc1ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Mar 2026 11:58:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8173428e-c627-11f0-8a97-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-11-19T215040Z-1288817315-RC2JFCAAYKQX-RTRMADP-3-META-PLATFORMS-YANN-LECUN.jpg">REUTERS - Yves Herman</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>France's second woman in space prepares for launch after 30-year wait</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260211-france-s-second-woman-in-space-prepares-for-launch-after-30-year-wait</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot is set to fly to the International Space Station on Friday, 13 February 2026. She will launch at around 11:00 CET from Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida as part of NASA's SpaceX Crew-12 mission. The launch was due to take place today, Thursday, but was postponed because of bad weather. They are due to dock with ISS on Saturday evening.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ca39828-05ba-11f1-8540-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-862c6t3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ca39828-05ba-11f1-8540-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-862c6t3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">641ab3fa-05bc-11f1-b041-d75fd3b8fcac</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Feb 2026 20:07:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ca39828-05ba-11f1-8540-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-862c6t3.jpg">© Photo by Valentine CHAPUIS / AFP</source><dc:creator>Dhananjay Khadilkar</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Why Europe's road to digital autonomy is long and winding</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260201-why-europe-s-road-to-digital-autonomy-is-long-and-winding</link><description>
Rising tensions with the United States are pushing the European Union to make moves towards autonomy – including in the digital field.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/53adbac8-b641-11f0-9756-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/INFOX-78.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/53adbac8-b641-11f0-9756-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/INFOX-78.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">233a67ce-fb88-11f0-b670-99a876a2c9f4</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Feb 2026 08:41:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/53adbac8-b641-11f0-9756-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/INFOX-78.png">© RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>France's Sophie Adenot to spend nine months on ISS after medical evacuation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260115-france-sophie-adenot-to-spend-nine-months-on-iss-after-medical-evacuation</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot’s first mission to the International Space Station is being brought forward and extended to nine months after an unprecedented medical evacuation forced a reshuffle of the station’s crew rota.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a40e6f36-ca1d-11f0-9e01-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/L-astronaute-fran%C3%A7aise-Sophie-Adenot-s-exprime-lors-d-une-conf%C3%A9rence-de-presse-concernant-son-d%C3%A9part-pour-la-Station-spatiale-internationale-ISS-en-2026-au-Centre-national-d-%C3%A9tudes-spatiales-CNES-%C3%A0-Toulouse-le-24-novembre.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a40e6f36-ca1d-11f0-9e01-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/L-astronaute-fran%C3%A7aise-Sophie-Adenot-s-exprime-lors-d-une-conf%C3%A9rence-de-presse-concernant-son-d%C3%A9part-pour-la-Station-spatiale-internationale-ISS-en-2026-au-Centre-national-d-%C3%A9tudes-spatiales-CNES-%C3%A0-Toulouse-le-24-novembre.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a1dcc34-f205-11f0-b240-4d9e41b08d26</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jan 2026 13:45:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a40e6f36-ca1d-11f0-9e01-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/L-astronaute-fran%C3%A7aise-Sophie-Adenot-s-exprime-lors-d-une-conf%C3%A9rence-de-presse-concernant-son-d%C3%A9part-pour-la-Station-spatiale-internationale-ISS-en-2026-au-Centre-national-d-%C3%A9tudes-spatiales-CNES-%C3%A0-Toulouse-le-24-novembre.jpg">AFP - VALENTINE CHAPUIS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>French firm part of global quest to build quantum computers</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260115-french-firm-part-of-global-quest-to-build-quantum-computers</link><description>
A century after quantum mechanics revolutionised physics, one of its most transformative applications, the quantum computer, is edging closer to reality. Among the global race of companies pursuing this technology, French startup Quandela is taking a distinctive approach from its headquarters in Massy, just outside Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cbffe788-f1ee-11f0-acde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Quandela-Giesz.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cbffe788-f1ee-11f0-acde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Quandela-Giesz.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3fb10b1c-f1ef-11f0-ad3d-7798599d24a2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jan 2026 12:28:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cbffe788-f1ee-11f0-acde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Quandela-Giesz.png">© RFI</source><dc:creator>Dhananjay Khadilkar</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>French scientists turn waste carbon into fuel using new catalyst</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20251217-french-scientists-turn-waste-carbon-into-fuel-using-new-catalyst</link><description>
French researchers have developed a breakthrough technology that could help tackle climate change whilst creating useful fuels from industrial waste. Dhananjay Khadilkar has this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/08b45fda-a9d1-11f0-9efe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20017315361958.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/08b45fda-a9d1-11f0-9efe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20017315361958.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93f53de6-db3e-11f0-bca2-dd57fbcf2f47</guid><pubDate>Wed, 17 Dec 2025 11:51:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/08b45fda-a9d1-11f0-9efe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20017315361958.jpg">AP - Michael Probst</source><dc:creator>Dhananjay Khadilkar</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>France's first woman in space in 25 years counts down to trip to the ISS</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20251130-france-first-woman-in-space-in-25-years-prepares-for-trip-to-the-iss-sophie-adenot</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot is preparing for her first mission to the International Space Station in February 2026, a trip that will make her the first Frenchwoman in space since 2001. During her eight-month stay, she will conduct nearly 200 scientific experiments in microgravity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a40e6f36-ca1d-11f0-9e01-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/L-astronaute-fran%C3%A7aise-Sophie-Adenot-s-exprime-lors-d-une-conf%C3%A9rence-de-presse-concernant-son-d%C3%A9part-pour-la-Station-spatiale-internationale-ISS-en-2026-au-Centre-national-d-%C3%A9tudes-spatiales-CNES-%C3%A0-Toulouse-le-24-novembre.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a40e6f36-ca1d-11f0-9e01-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/L-astronaute-fran%C3%A7aise-Sophie-Adenot-s-exprime-lors-d-une-conf%C3%A9rence-de-presse-concernant-son-d%C3%A9part-pour-la-Station-spatiale-internationale-ISS-en-2026-au-Centre-national-d-%C3%A9tudes-spatiales-CNES-%C3%A0-Toulouse-le-24-novembre.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a1a17fc-caac-11f0-9496-d7ea195d31fb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Nov 2025 14:08:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a40e6f36-ca1d-11f0-9e01-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/L-astronaute-fran%C3%A7aise-Sophie-Adenot-s-exprime-lors-d-une-conf%C3%A9rence-de-presse-concernant-son-d%C3%A9part-pour-la-Station-spatiale-internationale-ISS-en-2026-au-Centre-national-d-%C3%A9tudes-spatiales-CNES-%C3%A0-Toulouse-le-24-novembre.jpg">© AFP - VALENTINE CHAPUIS </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>From the Lab: ESA's  Solar Orbiter reveals sun's south pole for first time</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20251128-from-the-lab-esa-s-solar-orbiter-reveals-sun-s-south-pole-for-first-time</link><description>
The European Space Agency's Solar Orbiter spacecraft has achieved a groundbreaking milestone by capturing the first-ever detailed images of the sun's south pole earlier this year. This unprecedented view offers scientists a crucial new perspective on our closest star.
